sentences.l:
But may a power you
lead away home, and may you not meet that man,
when he comes back to his dear fatherland;

upon the daughter of Icarius sweet sleep she poured down,
and she slept, having leaned back, and all her limbs were loosened
there on the couch;

With beauty first her fine face she cleansed,
ambrosial, such as fair-crowned Cytherea
anoints herself with, whenever she goes to the dance of the Graces, full of longing;

She, then, having so done, went away, heavenly-one of goddesses,
and there came attendants, white-armed, out of the hall,
with a sound coming on;

And she, when now she reached the suitors, heavenly-one of women,
stood then beside the doorpost of the close-built roof,
before her cheeks holding her shining veil;
